+/**
+ * mem_reentrancy_guard_abort: release every MMIO re-entrancy guard engaged by
+ * the calling thread.
+ *
+ * Called by cpu_loop_exit() before the longjmp, while the access frames that
+ * engaged the guards are still live (their normal release path is skipped when
+ * the stack is unwound).  Without this a device stays marked engaged_in_io and
+ * the next access to it is rejected as re-entrant (ISS-064).
+ */
+void mem_reentrancy_guard_abort(void);
